          "text": "HSÜ Ching-ch'êng 許景澄 (T. 竹筠[篔], original ming 癸身 T. 拱辰), Oct. 22, 1845–1900, July 28, diplomat and liberal statesman, who died a martyr in the Boxer rebellion, was a native of Chia-hsing, Chekiang.",
